# Driver Forgot Password API - Test File
# This file contains ONLY the forgot password endpoints for clean testing

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/drivers
@driverEmail = skprasath@yopmail.com
@driverPassword = driver12334
@driverOtp = 123456

### ============================================
### FORGOT PASSWORD FLOW
### ============================================
### Instructions:
### 1. Run requests 1 → 2 → 3 in order
### 2. Then run request 4 to login with new password
### 3. Test OTP: Always use 123456 for testing
### ============================================

### 1) Send Forgot Password OTP
# This sends a 6-digit OTP to the driver's email
# In testing, you can use 123456 without checking email
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{driverEmail}}"
}

### 2) Verify Forgot Password OTP
# Use the OTP from email OR use 123456 for testing
# Must be run AFTER request 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{driverEmail}}",
  "otp": "{{driverOtp}}"
}

### 3) Set New Password
# Sets a new password for the driver
# Must be run AFTER request 2 (OTP verification)
POST {{baseUrl}}/forgot-password/set-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{driverEmail}}",
  "password": "{{driverPassword}}"
}

### 4) Login with New Password
# Test that the new password works
# @name forgotPasswordLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{driverEmail}}",
  "password": "{{driverPassword}}"
}

### ============================================
### EXPECTED RESPONSES
### ============================================

### Request 1 - Send OTP Success:
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "OTP sent successfully"
# }

### Request 1 - Driver Not Found Error:
# HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Driver not found"
# }

### Request 2 - Verify OTP Success:
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "OTP verified successfully"
# }

### Request 2 - Invalid OTP Error:
# HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Invalid OTP"
# }

### Request 2 - OTP Expired Error:
# HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "OTP has expired"
# }

### Request 3 - Set Password Success:
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Password reset successfully"
# }

### Request 3 - Not Verified Error:
# HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Email is not verified"
# }

### Request 4 - Login Success:
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# {
#   "token": "eyJhbGci...",
#   "user": {
#     "id": "...",
#     "name": "...",
#     "email": "skprasath@yopmail.com",
#     "role": "driver",
#     "status": "OFFLINE",
#     "is_blocked": false
#   }
# }

### ============================================
### TESTING WITH CURL
### ============================================

### Send OTP:
# curl -X POST http://192.168.1.16:3000/api/drivers/forgot-password/email \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"email":"skprasath@yopmail.com"}'

### Verify OTP:
# curl -X POST http://192.168.1.16:3000/api/drivers/forgot-password/verify-otp \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"email":"skprasath@yopmail.com","otp":"123456"}'

### Set Password:
# curl -X POST http://192.168.1.16:3000/api/drivers/forgot-password/set-password \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"email":"skprasath@yopmail.com","password":"driver12334"}'

### Login:
# curl -X POST http://192.168.1.16:3000/api/drivers/login \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"email":"skprasath@yopmail.com","password":"driver12334"}'

### ============================================
### COMMON ISSUES & SOLUTIONS
### ============================================

### Issue: 401 Unauthorized
# Solution: This should NOT happen. Forgot password endpoints are public.
# Check the URL is correct: /api/drivers/forgot-password/email

### Issue: OTP email not received
# Solution: Use test OTP "123456" - it always works for testing

### Issue: 400 Bad Request
# Solution: Check email format and OTP is 6 digits

### Issue: 404 Driver Not Found
# Solution: Verify email exists in database with role "DRIVER"

### Issue: OTP has expired
# Solution: Request a new OTP (run request 1 again)

